# Codex refresh review: envelope-kinematics-pv
VERDICT: FIX
REFRESH: PARTIAL

## Findings

- RR-01 | medium | stale | “X(C18O)…4e-8 to ~9e-7…8” | The retained lower bound misses 2.8e-8 in 2017ApJ...849...56A. The count omits explicit abundances in 2015ApJ...812..129Y, 2020ApJ...894...23H and 2025ApJ...995L...7L. | Include nominal and alternative abundances separately; lower the full range to 2.8e-8 and recount, with at least 11 qualifying papers.
- RR-02 | medium | stale | “Envelope density law…r^-1.5; r^-1.8…9” | The pack also gives indices -2 in 2015ApJ...812..129Y, approximately -0.13 in 2025ApJ...995L...7L and -2.5 in 2026AJ....172...75M. | Expand the range and recount under the stated scope; distinguish adopted laws from tested alternatives.
- RR-03 | medium | attribution | “Low-velocity exclusion…4”; “alpha…3” | The first count omits 2015ApJ...812..129Y, whose pack setting requires ΔV > 1.2 km/s. The second omits 2018ApJ...869L..24I, explicitly using 40% of free fall. | Increase the respective counts to at least five and four, then audit remaining qualifying entries.
- RR-04 | medium | attribution | “PV cut width…9 envelope and core papers” | 2019A&A...621A..83S supplies the 0.2-arcsec slit but is an NGC 1566 galaxy-outflow paper, per the pack title. Several other examples measure protostellar outflows rather than envelopes. | Separate generic extraction examples from envelope measurements and recompute the scoped count and range.
- RR-05 | medium | attribution | “Fit…in log R–log V…or orthogonal distance regression” | The 2026ApJ..1003..219W excerpt fits a signed velocity–position function with systemic velocity and positional offset; it does not describe a log–log ODR fit. | Describe that fit separately from the 2015/2017 log–log fits and retain its offset parameters.
- RR-06 | medium | attribution | “Model intrinsic line width…0.5 km/s…6” | For 2016ApJ...820L..34S, the pack says “convolved with 0.5 km/s velocity width,” which does not establish an intrinsic width. Other entries leave the width definition unspecified, whereas 2020ApJ...904..185O explicitly gives FWHM. | Separate intrinsic broadening from convolution width; record sigma/FWHM/unspecified and remove the interchangeable default.
- RR-07 | medium | lost-fix | “Centroid acceptance…SNR > 5 to > 10…2” | SR-03 explicitly separated channel-map astrometry from PV centroid acceptance. The current row merges them again: 2018ApJ...859..111H supplies astrometry SNR > 5, while 2022A&A...664A.171V supplies the Gaussian-centroid criteria. | Restore separate rows with count one each and keep their acceptance rules distinct.
- RR-08 | medium | usability | “Measure the rotation profile…the ‘ridge’ approach” | This heading groups intensity-weighted mean positions with SLAM ridge extraction. The 2023ApJ...958...98F excerpt defines SLAM ridge as the emission peak, distinct from a clipped intensity-weighted mean. | Name mean-position, Gaussian-centroid, ridge and edge extraction separately; associate thresholds and bias checks with each.
- RR-09 | medium | science | “p = 1 means rotation plus infall conserving angular momentum” | V_phi ∝ R^-1 establishes constant axial specific angular momentum, but does not establish radial motion. The pack’s 2017ApJ...834..178Y model assumes free-fall infall separately from constant angular momentum. | Say “consistent with conserved-j rotation”; require independent evidence or modeling for infall.
- RR-10 | medium | broken-edit | “Centrifugal barrier or radius” | The tables recombine quantities distinguished in Step 5. The pack gives r_c = l²/(GM) and r_0 = l²/(2GM) in 2017ApJ...843...27L; 2026ApJ..1003..219W labels 1300 au a centrifugal radius. | Split barrier and centrifugal-radius rows, and distinguish fitted values, limits and explored grids.
- RR-11 | medium | science | “t_ff = sqrt(R³ / 2GM*); then Mdot = M_streamer / t_ff” | This faithfully reproduces 2025ApJ...985..166K’s convention, but equals R/v_ff rather than a general trajectory travel time. Radial fall from rest at R takes π/2 times this value; rotation and initial velocity further change it. | Label it the paper’s characteristic timescale; use integrated trajectory travel times when deriving a trajectory-based rate.
- RR-12 | medium | science | “I the streamline integral of normalised density” | The 2026ApJ..1003..219W excerpt specifies a two-dimensional volume integration over radius and polar angle, not a line integral along a streamline. | Define I = ∫(rho/Mdot)dV, including 2πr²sin(theta), integration bounds and the adopted density normalization; put implementation details in parameters.md.
- RR-13 | medium | usability | “Correct the apparent break radius for resolution” | The pack reports source-specific corrections in 2015ApJ...812...27A and 2017ApJ...849...56A; it supplies no transferable correction factor. Its limitation says the method “may systematically underestimate” the radius. | Require source-specific synthetic recovery tests with matching resolution and extraction settings; identify the quoted corrections as examples.
- RR-14 | medium | omission | “Forward-model…compare with PV diagrams or the cube” | The general workflow requires uv filtering but omits explicit spatial and spectral resolution matching. The 2026ApJ..1003..219W assumption line requires both. | Require matching beam, spectral response, sampling and PV extraction for every model comparison.
- RR-15 | medium | usability | “major-axis PV (PA 42 deg)” | In parameters.md this loses the direction convention: the 2026ApJ..1003..219W excerpt specifies 42 degrees north-to-west, and its trajectory setting says clockwise from north. | Preserve that convention and convert before supplying a conventional east-of-north PA to extraction software.
- RR-16 | medium | omission | “point mass, disk mass neglected” | The assumption is stated without an applicability check. The pack includes envelope-dominated Class 0-like systems (2026A&A...713A.149V) and an 80-Msun envelope around a 60-Msun protostar (2026AJ....172...75M). | Require checking enclosed gas mass against central mass over the fitted radii before using point-mass masses or trajectories.
- RR-17 | low | length | “SKILL.md” | The skill exceeds roughly 300 lines; extensive per-paper examples duplicate parameters.md. | Move detailed grids, numerical examples, expanded software inventories and the long source-card list into references; retain the workflow and essential cautions.

## Notes
The 493-paper description, science-field aggregates and listed software counts match the rebuilt pack.
New SLAM, emcee, GILDAS and LIME attributions have pack support; their departure from the old reconciliation is not itself a regression.
PARTIAL reflects the retained abundance bound and incompletely refreshed parameter summaries.
